{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155189-2e-cults-and-integrity","id":1155189,"title":"[2E] Cults and Integrity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-02T14:27:35-07:00","id":1155189,"title":"[2E] Cults and Integrity","content":"Something that show up in my head from latest <b>American Horror Story</b> season titled \u2013 you guessed it \u2013 <b>Cult</b>. <br /> <br /> Cults are built to give people purpose. To show them what decisions to do. To show them the way. But why future cult members are lost in the first place? Because they suffered. Because they are overburdened with life. Because they \u2018lost their ground under feet\u2019. Sound\u2019s familiar, yes?<br /> <br /> It sound just like Integrity loss effect \u2013 because it is. Most cults members are those that lost their stability, their foundation \u2013 their Integrity dots \u2013 and now try to recover it, any means possible. And then comes future cult leader, with simple solutions, answers to ones doubts \u2013 things that GIVE you stability. You regain Integrity, but something is off \u2013 it does not feel like before. Leader and cult somehow changed you. His words somehow changed who you feel you are. He changed who you ARE.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> Most cult members are people that lost at least a dot of Integrity lately, having scores at 6 or below. Many have even lower scores. Life is stretching them \u2013 whatever reason it is \u2013 and cult leader just use it. He offers solution: \u2018Follow me and life will become stable ones again\u2019 \u2013 or however he put it there. Clue is that new member REGAINS his lost Integrity dot on next Breaking Point made in actions to follow ways of cult \u2013 only with it there is attached Persistent Condition, related to cults teaching. Or member can change one of his Aspirations to one represented by cults ideas \u2013 players choosing. Cult change you, piece by piece\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Interesting subtopic - If being in cult is all about regaining Integrity \u2013 what about cults gathered by supernatural element?</b> Group that shows powers of mystical artifact or human-looking monster still would simply lead to more decrease of Integrity in it\u2019s members/viewers when they are confronted with truly supernatural phenomena before their eyes. How would you describe the answer on this topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T16:56:32-07:00","id":1155224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155189-2e-cults-and-integrity#post1155189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If being in cult is all about regaining Integrity \u2013 what about cults gathered by supernatural element?[/B] Group that shows powers of mystical artifact or human-looking monster still would simply lead to more decrease of Integrity in it\u2019s members/viewers when they are confronted with truly supernatural phenomena before their eyes. How would you describe the answer on this topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of being blunt, real life cults don't have magic. Lots of CoD cults have power and influence that the majority of real life ones just don't have and can offer tangible benefits or threats. Also, that integrity lose from seeing the supernatural at the heart of the cult could easily be the thing that traps the cultist in the first place. The cult presents a supernatural element and then offers the person a simple answer to it.<br /> <br /> Also, not everyone wants their integrity back. Spiralling into madness trying to unravel a mystery is probably not totally uncommon (and bear in mind, it doesn't need to be all that common a trait). It's how most Awakened get their start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:23:26-07:00","id":1155254,"title":"","content":"IRL things are far less bleak, far less strange, there is no unnatural power to deal with, and brainwashing isn't at all like in fiction and conspiracy theories.<br /> <br /> But they actually feel quite that way for the ones involved. They are dragged into the cult, they start to believe in things. They sense their ground shaking and the cult serving as salvation for a lost sense of self. It is all too real for the people induced. So I see the point.<br /> <br /> Yet, I'm not sure if regaining Integrity should be the way. I do think, though, that stopping to lose it could.<br /> <br /> Now my mind id working in another option. Going to the core of the idea, the cult offers answers to the loss of Integrity. Not everyone needs that, but some people do. And the setting makes it clear that by choosing madness to unveil the truth isn't the default answer, but quite the opposite. Most people avoid having their idea of the world changed that much, even if it means ignoring evidence of the supernatural. Following a cult could be easily the way for such people to cling to Integrity when they can't ignore things anymore.<br /> <br /> On my suggestion, instead of making the character regain Integrity, the cult ease the brunt of Breaking Points. From just seeing an angel to performing human sacrifice, the cult takes what would be a Breaking Point for most people and says it is ok, and actually a good thing. It is counter-intuitive for most people, but is reassuring for someone who already had to go through such Breaking Points. Then the cult start testing your faith, and those tests make you go further through Breaking Points, but the cult also makes you harden against those Breaking Points. The cult also causes you to gain a new set of Breaking Points: the realization that it was all for naught. The character become a zealot to protect her own Integrity, because to deny the cult is to have to face all those Breaking Points again as such.<br /> <br /> Make for each cult a set of Premises. A premise is composed of a Breaking Point and a Rationalization, an explanation on why you should accept that BP in your life. The character is induced by the cult to face the Breaking Point. If the character fails, instead of loosing Integrity, the Breaking Point is replaced by the Rationalization. If the character succeeds, it remains and consequences set themselves as normal, but the character can choose to try again later. If a character lost an Integrity dot before, this person can choose to embrace a Rationalization for the Breaking Point in question without this process.<br /> <br /> The catch is that Rationalizations are linked together in the beliefs of the cult. They form a whole, and only make sense together. If a character suffer a Breaking Point against a Rationalization, it gets the Condition &quot;Existential Doubt&quot;. During this, both all the Rationalizations and their respective Breaking Points become BPs for the character, but at +3 dice to resist. The character must go through a reassuring ritual with the cult to shed the Condition, probably something similar to what was used to set the challenged Rationalization. Or the character can shed the Condition by Denial of the cult. After a failed test to acquire a Rationalization the character can also get &quot;Existential Doubt&quot;.<br /> <br /> Denying the cult is simple, but hard. If the character does so, all the avoided Breaking Points fall at once on the Integrity score. It can led to several overlapping Conditions, and even to several dots of Integrity being lost at once. To shatter ones worldview can lead to madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}